  "notes": "{不思議|ふしぎ} functions as both a na-adjective (strange, mysterious) and a noun (wonder, mystery).\n\nFORMS:\n- Na-adjective: {不思議|ふしぎ}な + noun\n- Adverbial: {不思議|ふしぎ}に\n- Noun: {不思議|ふしぎ}\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- {不思議|ふしぎ}なことに: strangely enough\n- {不思議|ふしぎ}に{思|おも}う: to find strange\n- {不思議|ふしぎ}な{気持|きも}ち: a strange feeling\n- {七|なな}{不思議|ふしぎ}: seven wonders/mysteries\n\nCOLLOCATIONS:\n- {不思議|ふしぎ}な{力|ちから}: mysterious power\n- {不思議|ふしぎ}な{現象|げんしょう}: strange phenomenon\n- {自然|しぜん}の{不思議|ふしぎ}: wonders of nature\n\nCULTURAL NOTE:\n{不思議|ふしぎ}の{国|くに}のアリス = \"Alice in Wonderland\"\n\nThe word conveys a sense of puzzlement or wonder at something beyond ordinary understanding.",
